Z||000005||Formula88||11-29-2001||09:48 PM||||Check it out -- there's more than just the Fiero forum that is useful to us.  They have an entire forum dedicated to 60* V6 engines!  Not to mention 3400DOHC modifications, etc.  Not much traffic right now, but a good resource.<P>I especially liked the Citation X-11 forum.  They're talking about how the X-11 2.8 is the highest revving V6 GM has ever made, even higher than the 3.4DOHC, easily revving to 8000rpm stock.  Um, wasn't that engine the basis for the L44 V6 in the Fiero, only it was carbed?  They may have some more tech info that could help us. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||11-29-2001||10:01 PM||||Ok, there are some cool people on the X-11 forum.  They're talking about how great and universal the engine cradle is - and how you can swap in a Northstar into your Citation!!  <P>Sounds like they need to be turned onto Fieros, so they can go fast in a straight line AND corner.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
